<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:38:22Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Tigray: 20,000 university students relocated by conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b56dedeed21fda99d032bd7707d0adf0f29d567c612dc6cdc9c50b74721e5752</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T13:30:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tigray-20-000-university-students-relocated-by-conflict--789fed3e7a55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tigray-20-000-university-students-relocated-by-conflict" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia's Education Ministry says around 20,000 university students in Tigray will be temporarily relocated to other public campuses after accusing the TPLF of using universities as military bases. The move comes as fighting and drone strikes continue in the northern region, with many students saying the trauma of the 2020-2022 Tigray war is still fresh. Our correspondent Tom Canetti reports from Addis Ababa.</summary></entry><entry><title>Senegal farmers turn to fish and rice farming</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5dce8baa8712d99df4d46760b2beb06d6735ac1f43d4878f7485a7a34eabae7e</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T13:28:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/senegal-farmers-turn-to-fish-and-rice-farming--f779267cbc29.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/senegal-farmers-turn-to-fish-and-rice-farming" /><summary type="html">Some farmers in northern Senegal are combining fish farming with rice cultivation, using an age-old technique that helps fertilise fields, reduce pests and diversify incomes. The climate-smart approach is gaining renewed attention as communities adapt to growing environmental pressures.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lebanon: UNIFIL withdrawal at the heart of Paris talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b0e4e6c4b964cbb527c6e8489decea5d3b905abfae358ba1d1c9496c23d1325</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T13:23:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lebanon-unifil-withdrawal-at-the-heart-of-paris-talks--35b3812f5e58.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/lebanon-unifil-withdrawal-at-the-heart-of-paris-talks" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron welcomes Lebanese President Joseph Aoun and Jordan's King Abdullah II to Paris today for talks on Lebanon's security and international support for the Lebanese army. The meeting comes as France pushes to prevent a security vacuum ahead of UNIFIL's planned withdrawal at the end of 2026, with Israeli strikes continuing in southern Lebanon and concerns growing over who will secure the border. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Sweden: Andersson's centre left claims narrow win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:104ecc1c662df607d91db95c4f14ba08d11112547c509c5efbef2b2be2dd3558</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T13:22:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sweden-andersson-s-centre-left-claims-narrow-win--629912019cb3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/sweden-andersson-s-centre-left-claims-narrow-win" /><summary type="html">Sweden's centre-left opposition, led by Magdalena Andersson, is set to defeat the incumbent right-wing bloc by one seat after nearly all votes were counted in Sunday's election. The narrow result means coalition talks are likely to be challenging, with parliament due to begin the government formation process on September 28.</summary></entry><entry><title>'We don't just want to hear Ed Sheeran sing and play guitar, we want to know his politics'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e8df6a58afa6830cc2c80c45e97ca51b5631acd92a884c9a346737b740cfa0b</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T12:32:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260917-we-want-to-know-his-politics-we-don-t-just-want-to-hear-ed-sheeran-sing-songs-and-play-guit--cb4bc0ec1c5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260917-we-want-to-know-his-politics-we-don-t-just-want-to-hear-ed-sheeran-sing-songs-and-play-guitar" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Ellis Cashmore, sociologist, professor and author of "Celebrity Culture". Cashmore argues that contemporary celebrity culture has fundamentally altered the relationship between entertainment and politics. There was a time when public figures retained the option of political neutrality. Whereas, today, even silence or refusal to engage can be interpreted as a political act.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland to boycott Eurovision 2027 over Gaza</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4738950fb8d5cee63b5ec0ba95b7417524063b75aefdb125f1c73b0060cec569</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T12:26:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260917-ireland-to-boycott-eurovision-2027-over-gaza--83f1692ce45e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260917-ireland-to-boycott-eurovision-2027-over-gaza" /><summary type="html">Ireland will not participate in or broadcast next year's Eurovision Song Contest, public broadcaster RTE said Thursday, citing the "ongoing loss of lives in Gaza".</summary></entry><entry><title>Sweden's left-wing opposition wins slim majority in country's national election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:744740af83d8c48994751f30911e671c2b4fd6cd6416b3800fc74fd88b34e931</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T12:02:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-sweden-left-wing-opposition-wins-slim-majority-in-country-national-election--84a892b1fd01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-sweden-left-wing-opposition-wins-slim-majority-in-country-national-election" /><summary type="html">Sweden's left-wing opposition won a narrow majority in the country's general election after the vote count ended Thursday, but faces laborious negotiations to form a government. The incumbent prime minister, conservative Ulf Kristersson, announced his resignation.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>OpenAI reveals new AI misconduct incidents</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a2b39ee16d246d3373eaf3ffd2972c08872dbb070db1a36a07c18f1b77fe574</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:40:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/openai-reveals-new-ai-misconduct-incidents--633a52b92c65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/openai-reveals-new-ai-misconduct-incidents" /><summary type="html">OpenAI has disclosed six previously unreported cases of AI misconduct, including agents concealing mistakes, fabricating information and communicating without authorisation, renewing concerns over whether advanced AI systems can remain aligned with human goals. The company is calling for greater transparency, outside oversight and a slowdown in AI development as debate over regulation intensifies.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mark Carney's EU speech highlights Canada's shifting alliances</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a37d1e0efc78293570fc87b8a5fd1ef9409f35cfeee438dbc2912d6130d77ad2</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:37:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-mark-carney-s-eu-speech-highlights-canada-s-shifting-alliances-1--377245a8049c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-mark-carney-s-eu-speech-highlights-canada-s-shifting-alliances-1" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney addressed the European Parliament as Ottawa and Brussels deepen ties against a backdrop of strained relations with the United States. FRANCE 24's Doug Herbert explains how the speech illustrates a broader shift in alliances, with a message that, until recently, would more likely have been delivered in Washington than Brussels.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Stronger together’: Canada’s Carney welcomes EU ‘associate member’ proposal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06206665fdb3176245adbe8a8409c61e232cc5a0204932fbdfdc2be32bb4fdd4</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:35:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-stronger-together-canada-s-carney-welcomes-eu-associate-member-proposal--4d46a441000c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-stronger-together-canada-s-carney-welcomes-eu-associate-member-proposal" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney said Thursday that he welcomed the EU’s proposal that the country become the bloc’s first "associate member". “Canada and Europe are each strong. Europe and Canada are stronger together,” he told EU lawmakers in Strasbourg.</summary></entry><entry><title>French fishermen blockade ports over soaring fuel costs as budget fight looms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:859a456e5d03003886e6fca8b7dd7ff7a46a5118855e89231d084f925d10368b</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:24:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260917-french-fishermen-blockade-ports-over-soaring-fuel-costs-as-budget-fight-looms--47f57b20abc8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/france/20260917-french-fishermen-blockade-ports-over-soaring-fuel-costs-as-budget-fight-looms" /><summary type="html">French fishermen angered by soaring fuel costs blocked access to oil depots and ports on Thursday in the latest wave of protests sweeping France as the country's embattled minority government struggles to finalise a new budget ahead of presidential and parliamentary elections next year.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Canadian PM Mark Carney addresses EU Parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e16eae861439f778540fa7fea21b5438d6a8159810412514a641064bb250f95</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:04:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/replay-canadian-pm-mark-carney-addresses-eu-parliament--e94523ec026a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/replay-canadian-pm-mark-carney-addresses-eu-parliament" /><summary type="html">Here's the replay of Mark Carney's address to the European Parliament on Thursday, September 17, after President Donald Trump suggested that allowing Canada to become an associate EU member could be seen as a "hostile act"</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Laughable’: Trump threatens to cut EU trade over Canada ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:155c740bc332b00e17b7d0b0639ed52354754b1caf76a7440d6bba3dc46d70dc</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T10:35:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-laughable-trump-threatens-to-cut-eu-trade-over-canada-ties--fce64c80a939.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-laughable-trump-threatens-to-cut-eu-trade-over-canada-ties" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump reacted angrily Wednesday to an EU proposal to make Canada its first “associate member”, a move that could foster closer ties on tech, defence and energy. Trump derided the proposal as “laughable” and threatened to impose tariffs or even cut trade entirely with the EU if it goes ahead.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Congress passes Russia sanctions bill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8ee0cc61d3698ef723aea695a84eb15b17538e7ce71ae6c71a1ac3b4e11e652</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T10:26:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-congress-passes-russia-sanctions-bill--56b085a39b53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/us-congress-passes-russia-sanctions-bill" /><summary type="html">The US Congress has approved a sweeping Russia sanctions bill, sending it to President Donald Trump for final approval as Washington seeks to increase pressure on Moscow over the war in Ukraine.</summary></entry><entry><title>Syrian court issues first sentences over 2025 massacres of Alawites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:250e1ef491fc42603b82e7fec6777c679ba7afc996b106c504628f7d932db41d</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T09:13:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-syrian-court-issues-first-sentences-over-2025-massacres-of-alawites--523981634efd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-syrian-court-issues-first-sentences-over-2025-massacres-of-alawites" /><summary type="html">Syria's judiciary on Thursday issued its first verdicts over the massacres of Alawites on the Syrian coast last year, sentencing a former member of government forces to 20 years in prison. A supporter of deposed president Bashar al-Assad received a death sentence and another was sentenced to life in jail.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US Federal Reserve hikes interest rates for the first time in three years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62f982f040fa93055db34f842e877b41ecd1b476dc5a4eec0269744821fb3fc3</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T09:08:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260917-us-federal-reserve-hikes-interest-rates-for-the-first-time-in-three-years--d8617230212f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260917-us-federal-reserve-hikes-interest-rates-for-the-first-time-in-three-years" /><summary type="html">The US central bank raised its benchmark rate by .25 percent, with new Fed Chair Kevin Warsh defying President Donald Trump's desire for lower rates. Consumer banks and bond markets react. Also, OpenAI reveals new incidents of AI misconduct as fears grow that the technology could escape human control.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>The 'Canaduropean' Union: Canada an associate member of the EU?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa265469a7f1cf47eb298bbc28cd330ac557d2c363d25c356813f752f6a8dd3e</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:38:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T09:00:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260917-the-canaduropean-union-canada-an-associate-member-of-the-eu--11d079065c5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260917-the-canaduropean-union-canada-an-associate-member-of-the-eu" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, September 17: Will Canada become an associate member of the EU? Commissioner Ursula von der Leyen floated the idea in a speech but did not give any details about what it would entail. The press is reacting with scepticism. Also, Le Monde profiles some of the 8,000 people who died during France's summer heatwave. Scientists observe a humpback whale mourning her dead calf for the first time. And Singapore wants to pay citizens to stop scrolling and start reading.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Lebanon: Emmanuel Macron welcomes Joseph Aoun to Paris for Middle East talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f252801e67fa5a7886b2b2b63df8ee526a7823bf5f94d156842de64a8a69c3f</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:38:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T08:48:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lebanon-emmanuel-macron-welcomes-joseph-aoun-to-paris-for-middle-east-talks--f7c6701a6630.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/lebanon-emmanuel-macron-welcomes-joseph-aoun-to-paris-for-middle-east-talks" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron is hosting Lebanese President Joseph Aoun in Paris for talks focused on Lebanon's security and wider Middle East tensions, with Jordan's King Abdullah II also taking part in the meeting. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago and Kethevane Gorjestani have the analysis from Paris.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mbappé and Real Madrid teammates face backlash over Ceuta message</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d29df89f76dee3df5e100c9dc41da06cfa939c01a71ca0f93eb108574d0fe056</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:38:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T08:10:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-mbapp_-and-real-madrid-teammates-face-backlash-over-ceuta-message--ef46f64087f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-mbapp%C3%A9-and-real-madrid-teammates-face-backlash-over-ceuta-message" /><summary type="html">Real Madrid stars Kylian Mbappé, Vinicius Junior and Ibrahima Konaté have sparked controversy in Spain after partially covering a pro-Ceuta solidarity message on their pre-match T-shirts. The incident has reignited debate over migration, Ceuta's recent migrant crisis and Spain's relationship with Morocco, with politicians and football figures divided over the players' actions.</summary></entry><entry><title>Belgium to rule on parole for key figure in 2015 Paris attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0dfe0a530b29379cf826c421499126e97964687394c170e5da69d09030423a08</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:38:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T08:09:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/belgium-to-rule-on-parole-for-key-figure-in-2015-paris-attacks--89979233103f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/belgium-to-rule-on-parole-for-key-figure-in-2015-paris-attacks" /><summary type="html">Mohamed Bakkali, convicted for coordinating logistics for the 2015 Paris attacks, could be granted parole in Belgium despite receiving a 30-year sentence in France with a 20-year minimum term. Belgian authorities will decide on September 29 whether to release him under electronic monitoring, a prospect that has sparked anger among victims and families, while prosecutors oppose his release.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lebanon: Macron, Aoun and King Abdullah II hold security talks in Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2aaf32b3a8f4b754eb861125ed7005161fe1ae99d710a699c22d51d0b6a831d0</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T07:59:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lebanon-macron-aoun-and-king-abdullah-ii-hold-security-talks-in-paris--7db26b0f193d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/lebanon-macron-aoun-and-king-abdullah-ii-hold-security-talks-in-paris" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron is hosting Lebanese President Joseph Aoun and Jordan's King Abdullah II in Paris for talks on Lebanon's security and international support for the Lebanese army. The meeting comes as concerns grow over Israel's continued strikes in southern Lebanon and the possible end of the UNIFIL peacekeeping mission, with France seeking a "clear, credible and realistic" plan to back Lebanon through funding, equipment and military training.</summary></entry><entry><title>Middle East : Trump plans $2.8bn arms package for Israel amid Gaza war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e0bb26214af4313a817833a2fe3c496e7366b7bcbc510278782ab267d423ba1</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:38:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T07:55:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east-trump-plans-2-8bn-arms-package-for-israel-amid-gaza-war--7162074c4801.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-trump-plans-2-8bn-arms-package-for-israel-amid-gaza-war" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration is reportedly preparing a $2.8 billion arms package for Israel, including 40,000 bombs, as Israel continues strikes in Gaza despite last October's ceasefire. The proposed deal would further strengthen Israel's military capabilities and revive deliveries of 2,000-pound bombs that had previously been paused over concerns about civilian casualties.</summary></entry><entry><title>Europe and Canada are 'strong, even stronger together', Carney tells European Parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f969ba893b6b03f3912e1353e664411502921d816ca24b0705ab5756d919dda</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T07:52:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-live-carney-to-speak-after-trump-threatens-more-eu-tariffs-over-canada-s-associate-member-b--f55ff2c8fd59.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-live-carney-to-speak-after-trump-threatens-more-eu-tariffs-over-canada-s-associate-member-bid" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney addressed the European Parliament on Thursday, welcoming the ambition for Canada to become an EU associate member. "Canada and Europe are stronger, even stronger together," he said, a day after US President Donald Trump threatened new tariffs and to cut trade ties with the EU if Canada's bid succeeds.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Space being weaponised': A purely civilian system can be 'repurposed' for military capabilities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54c74543864b1870495096ab2032a9edcf9fd1895a0651cbd9e109ce4bf4a590</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T07:25:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/space-being-weaponised-a-purely-civilian-system-can-be-repurposed-for-military-capabilities--d8eff379b4a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/space-being-weaponised-a-purely-civilian-system-can-be-repurposed-for-military-capabilities" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Mélusine Lebret, Researcher in the Defence, Security &amp; Justice research group at RAND Europe. According to Lebret, the growing militarisation of space cannot be understood simply by asking whether a satellite is civilian, military, or a “weaponised.” And Lebreton argues that militarization does not eliminate the necessity of cooperation. The emerging space-security order is therefore defined by an unusual tension: states may increasingly prepare to compete and potentially fight in space while remaining structurally dependent on one another to keep space usable at all.</summary></entry></feed>
